.env
# Backups and variants of it are the same secrets in a different filename.
# `.env.example` is the tracked template and stays tracked (negated below).
.env.*
!.env.example
data/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store

# Boss portraits are game assets; the README explains what to drop in.
config/portraits/*
!config/portraits/README.md

.claude

# The live persona is deployment flavour text: it names a character and the
# guild's in-jokes, it is edited far more often than code, and it belongs on the
# data volume (`data/` above is already ignored). Only the template is tracked.
persona.md
persona-*.md
!persona.example.md

# The design spec is kept locally rather than published.
DESIGN.md
